{"version":1,"type":"session-summary","driving_event":"Issue #631 requires a local ACP Runtime to reject non-v2 initialization and expose the complete advertised capabilities and instance configuration identity; the current backend discarded unknown capability fields and did not publish RuntimeInstance discovery objects.","decision":"Keep process ownership in ACPAscendantBackend, reject unsupported protocol negotiation as a lifecycle failure, preserve raw initialize capabilities, derive a versioned launch fingerprint from command, arguments, and environment names, and publish RuntimeInstance objects with Node ID and health.","impact":"Adds public fields and snapshot access to GnosticProtocol and GnosticCore, and adds RuntimeInstance discovery/subscription to the Node network surface. Environment values remain excluded from the fingerprint. No dependency changes. The public contract requires independent review before merge.","recurrence_control":"Regression tests cover wrong ACP versions, unknown nested capability fields, secret-free fingerprint stability, runtime health recovery, object serialization, Node-scoped advertisement, and subscription lifecycle; make verify and all smoke gates pass.","rejected_alternatives":["Keep only typed capability fields and lose unknown extensions.","Expose Runtime metadata only locally while leaving the Node discovery surface unaware of RuntimeInstance objects.","Add a parallel generic process supervisor despite the existing ACP process owner and its lifecycle tests."],"sources":[]}
